title: Linux Bubblewrap Sandbox Spike Tasks
status: draft
created: 2026-10-31
author: adrian
items[17]{id,title,description,criteria,complexity,effort,dependencies,refs}:
  T-001,"Scratch layout","Create `adrs/2026-10-31-linux-bwrap-sandbox/poc` with `bwrap` and `fixture` subdirectories. Each Cargo.toml carries an empty `[workspace]` table so neither crate joins the agentkit workspace, and no agentkit crate references them.","`cargo metadata` at the repo root does not list either package; removing the ADR directory leaves the workspace buildable.",low,0.5h,,"spike-only"
  T-002,"Typed view and argv builder","Represent the view as types: workspace, read-only paths, writable paths, environment, and a fixed namespace set. Render bwrap argv from the model, and keep the builder free of shell interpolation.","A unit test asserts that a view renders a stable argv and that no argument is produced by joining caller-supplied strings.",medium,3h,T-001,"argument-construction,namespace-set,filesystem-view"
  T-003,"Canonicalisation and invariants","Canonicalise every path with `std::fs::canonicalize` before rendering, reject relative paths and paths escaping the workspace, and apply invariants the caller cannot widen: no host home, store read-only, workspace the only writable tree, network namespace always unshared.","A symlinked path renders resolved; a path escaping the workspace is rejected; a request to mount the host home or the store read-write is refused.",medium,2h,T-002,"path-canonicalisation,invariant-rules"
  T-004,"Version floor and fail closed","Parse `bwrap --version`, refuse to run below the floor required by the emitted flags, and exit non-zero without execing when bwrap is missing, too old, or a namespace cannot be created.","The exact exit code is asserted for a missing binary, an old version and a blocked user namespace; the command sentinel is absent in each case.",medium,2h,T-002,"version-floor,fail-closed,bwrap-missing-or-old"
  T-005,"Fixture crate","A small Rust crate that builds and tests, materialised into the workspace before each run.","`cargo build` and `cargo test` both succeed inside the sandbox with the store readable and the workspace writable.",medium,2h,T-001,"shared-command-app,research-scenarios"
  T-006,"Hostile checks","Add the adversarial half of the fixture: a write outside the workspace, a write inside the host home, a read of a credential file, an outbound connection, and a child process that repeats the write. Each check reports whether the write landed.","Every hostile check reports the operation blocked and leaves no artefact on the host; a deliberately over-broad view makes at least one report a leak.",medium,2h,T-005,"write-outside-workspace-denied,credential-read-denied,descendants-confined,network-denied-by-default"
  T-007,"First end-to-end run","Run the fixture under the harness with the initial bind set and record the raw output, the argv, and every failure.","The fixture crate builds and tests; all hostile checks are blocked; every failure is listed with the missing path or namespace that caused it.",medium,2h,"T-003,T-004,T-005,T-006","shared-command-app"
  T-008,"Baseline iteration","Add the paths a Nix-built toolchain needs, discovered by failure: the store, the system profile on NixOS, the dynamic linker, and the certificate, hosts and resolver files. Attribute each addition to the observation that required it.","A table in the findings maps each added path to the failure it fixed; removing it reproduces the failure.",medium,3h,T-007,"toolchain-baseline,nixos-system-profile"
  T-009,"Isolation assertions","Prove the store is read-only, the host home is absent from the view, and host processes are invisible and unsignalable.","Writing to the store fails while executing from it succeeds; the host home path does not resolve; a kill against a host pid fails.",medium,2h,T-007,"store-read-only,host-home-absent,host-pids-hidden"
  T-010,"Lifecycle","Make each sandbox its own session and process group and exercise pause, resume and delete against a command that keeps working. Count survivors after the kill.","The written byte count is unchanged while paused, increases after resume, and no child survives the group kill; the behaviour of a `setsid` escape is recorded.",high,3h,T-007,"process-group-lifecycle,pause-and-resume,delete-kills-and-cleans,process-group-escape"
  T-011,"Denial diagnostics","Establish what an operator sees when a command is blocked: errno in the child, whether the path is absent or permission-denied, and what bwrap or the kernel logged.","A written note states what is observable, what is not, and how a blocked command is distinguished from one that failed for its own reasons.",medium,2h,T-007,"denial-diagnostics,explainable-failures"
  T-012,"Portability matrix","Run the user namespace probe on NixOS, Fedora and Ubuntu, including Ubuntu's default AppArmor restriction, and record the exact command and result for each.","Each distribution has a row with kernel version, the probe command and its output; Ubuntu's restricted case records the remediation.",medium,2h,T-004,"portability-matrix,userns-restricted"
  T-013,"Cost measurement","Time argv construction plus bwrap plus exec against a bare exec baseline and record median and p95.","A table reports both figures with the baseline column and the number of runs.",low,1h,T-007,"startup-cost"
  T-014,"Golden arguments","Store the rendered argv for a small set of views as fixtures and compare byte for byte.","Two fixtures cover a minimal view and a view with additional read paths; editing the builder fails the test until the fixture is updated.",low,1.5h,T-002,"golden-arguments,testability"
  T-015,"Edge checks","Exercise the edge cases that are cheap to confirm: a setuid binary, a device node outside the view, a nested bwrap, an unavailable cgroup namespace, and a command that exits leaving grandchildren.","Each case has a recorded observation and, where the behaviour is a limitation, a line in the findings.",medium,2h,T-007,"setuid-binaries,device-nodes,nested-bwrap,cgroup-namespace-unavailable,zombie-reaping,proc-mount-failure"
  T-016,"Findings and assessment","Write `findings.md`: per goal, the observation with the raw output, the gap, and the open risk. Add the qualitative judgement of the argv builder, configuration effort and maintainability.","Every goal in the spec has an answer with evidence; the recommendation states whether a production implementation is worth building and what it must own.",medium,3h,"T-008,T-009,T-010,T-011,T-012,T-013,T-015","findings-document,qualitative-assessment,findings-answer-questions,judgement-over-metrics"
  T-017,"Teardown check","Confirm the harness is unreachable from the rest of the suite, then record what would have to be removed to discard the spike.","No agentkit crate references the prototype, the Docker path still builds and its tests pass, and the removal steps are written down.",low,1h,T-016,"no-behaviour-change-elsewhere,docker-path-unaffected,spike-only,primitive-longevity"
